# Commit message in chat

After each completed task, include a ready-to-use git commit message in the chat reply.

- Put it near the end of the reply, clearly labeled (for example **Commit message**).
- 1–2 sentences that focus on why, not a file list.
- Cover only the work from that task.
- Do not run `git commit` unless the user explicitly asks to commit.
- Do this in addition to appending the task to `docs/process.md`.
